WEBVTT

00:00:14.206 --> 00:00:14.819
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Meet Tom.

00:00:15.528 --> 00:00:18.422
Like everyone, Tom likes to get a good night’s sleep.

00:00:20.796 --> 00:00:25.057
And like us all, Tom has about five separate dreams every night.

00:00:27.165 --> 00:00:30.749
These dreams can last between fifteen and forty minutes.

00:00:32.842 --> 00:00:36.297
According to experts, our dreams tell us who we are,

00:00:36.964 --> 00:00:39.407
what we need, and what we believe in,

00:00:40.494 --> 00:00:46.600
so, for Tom and for everyone else, here is a guide to the most common dreams and their meanings.

00:00:57.641 --> 00:01:00.962
<b>Dream one:</b> Somebody is running after you.

00:01:09.624 --> 00:01:14.005
If you have this dream, it means something is worrying you in real life.

00:01:15.389 --> 00:01:20.476
Something like a difficult decision or a difficult situation with a friend or a colleague.

00:01:26.392 --> 00:01:30.718
People often have this dream again and again until they make the decision

00:01:30.907 --> 00:01:33.313
or deal with the situation that is worrying them.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.393
<b>Dream two:</b> You can’t find something you need.

00:02:13.858 --> 00:02:18.350
Dreaming about losing something and trying to find it again is surprisingly common.

00:02:20.522 --> 00:02:24.959
It usually means that you’re worried about something stressful that you need to do soon,

00:02:25.371 --> 00:02:28.441
like going on a long journey or giving a talk in public.

00:02:37.779 --> 00:02:43.022
In these situations, people sometimes dream about losing their passport or tickets,

00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:45.897
or losing their notes or memory stick.

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:14.138
<b>Dream three:</b> You’re unprepared for an exam.

00:03:23.399 --> 00:03:29.986
This dream is common for young adults or children who are under stress, and it can feel very real –

00:03:42.393 --> 00:03:47.078
sometimes you can wake up sure that you’ve just failed an important exam or test.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.072
If you’re not doing any exams in real life,

00:03:59.409 --> 00:04:04.513
this dream could mean that you don’t have enough confidence in your ability to do something.

00:04:25.513 --> 00:04:29.127
<b>Dream four:</b> You’re flying or falling.

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:40.285
Another very common dream is the flying dream.

00:04:42.264 --> 00:04:45.287
Sometimes people dream that they are in control.

00:04:47.948 --> 00:04:51.854
If you feel in control, it means that your life is successful –

00:04:54.245 --> 00:04:58.640
perhaps you’ve just passed an important exam, or your boss has given you a promotion.

00:05:09.129 --> 00:05:13.211
But usually, people dream that they’re out of control and falling.

00:05:15.766 --> 00:05:19.806
This means the opposite – your life isn’t going well,

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:23.137
and you’re worried about what’s going to happen in the future.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.000
<b>Dream five:</b> You’re under water.

00:05:51.271 --> 00:05:53.201
If you dream that you’re under water,

00:05:53.345 --> 00:05:56.698
but you’re feeling happy and comfortable and you can still breathe,

00:05:57.412 --> 00:06:00.562
it could mean you have very strong feelings for someone.

00:06:05.041 --> 00:06:06.477
You’re probably in love!

00:06:26.274 --> 00:06:32.299
Sometimes dreams come true, but more often, they don’t!

00:06:45.289 --> 00:06:47.437
Sweet dreams!